  "story": {
    "id": "jamal_curb_contest",
    "person_id": "jamal_okonkwo",
    "title": "Contest at the curb",
    "summary": "Jamal races a lunch drop when a sidewalk bot and a robotaxi both claim the same curb — wariness turns into a near-miss calculation.",
    "beats": [
      {
        "id": "setup",
        "text": "Jamal clips into the pedals with two bags left and a timer that does not care about sidewalk etiquette. The restaurant curb is his usual grab-and-go; he has already lost three minutes to a road closure.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "approach",
        "text": "He cuts the alley shortcut the same way Elena avoids it — faster, not safer. Ahead he sees amber lights: a sidewalk bot holding the strip and a robotaxi rolling in for a passenger pickup.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "encounter",
        "text": "The loading strip is full. The bot blinks a status he cannot decode; the taxi door starts to open. Jamal has nowhere legal to stop without blocking either machine or the bike lane behind him.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "reaction",
        "text": "He brakes hard, chooses a half-meter gap, and commits. The bot lurches forward a foot. Jamal swerves, plants a foot on the pavement, and nearly clips a passenger's suitcase. His wariness spikes into anger — not at the machines themselves, but at the missing rulebook.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "outcome",
        "text": "He completes the pickup late and files a voice note to dispatch: skip dual-robot corners at lunch. Comfort settles back toward wary, not avoidant — he still needs the city to work with robots; he just refuses to be the collision-avoidance system for both of them.\n"
      }
    ],
